// Title: Potentially Suspicious Call To Win32_NTEventlogFile Class
// Sigma ID: caf201a9-c2ce-4a26-9c3a-2b9525413711
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-07-13 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment
// Description: Detects usage of the WMI class "Win32_NTEventlogFile" in a potentially suspicious way (delete,
//   backup, change permissions, etc.) from a PowerShell script
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/desktop/legacy/aa394225(v=vs.85)
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_nteventlogfile_usage.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "Win32_NTEventlogFile" and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".BackupEventlog(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ChangeSecurityPermissions(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ChangeSecurityPermissionsEx(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ClearEventLog(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".Delete(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".DeleteEx(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".Rename(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".TakeOwnerShip(" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".TakeOwnerShipEx(")
